1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,519
It's my first time ever here in ireland and there are some interesting things that I noticed in my first few days staying in dublin.
这是我第一次来爱尔兰，在都柏林住的头几天，我注意到一些有意思的事。

2
00:00:08,519 --> 00:00:22,680
The first thing is that it's really so green it's like everywhere you look there's green whether it's part of nature or green lights green paint green houses green is everywhere and it's really beautiful.
首先，这里真的很绿，目之所及都是绿色：自然景色、绿灯、绿漆、绿色房子，处处都是，很漂亮。

3
00:00:22,680 --> 00:00:27,960
But I was just very taken aback by hal green ireland really is.
但爱尔兰居然这么绿，还是让我很吃惊；hal 为来源不确定原词。

4
00:00:27,960 --> 00:00:35,280
Another thing that I noticed really quickly is how expensive it is especially compared to the rest of Europe.
另一件我很快注意到的事，是这里很贵，尤其与欧洲其他地方相比。

5
00:00:35,280 --> 00:00:46,490
And I've heard this is mostly within dublin and that once you get outside of the city that the prices are a lot more reasonable in the villages and smaller towns throughout the country.
我听说主要是都柏林这样，出了城，全国的村庄和小城镇价格会合理得多。

6
00:00:46,500 --> 00:00:52,020
So I'm here in ennis scary at the powers court house and gardens.
我现在在 Ennis Scary 的 Powers Court House and Gardens；地名和景点名为自动字幕待核。

7
00:00:52,020 --> 00:00:59,579
And I can say that you notice even 30 minutes or an hour outside of dublin that the prices do start to go down.
我能说，离都柏林只有三十分钟或一小时路程，就能注意到价格确实开始下降。

8
00:00:59,579 --> 00:01:04,500
But dublin is a city that's known for having very high housing prices.
但都柏林是以住房价格很高而闻名的城市。

9
00:01:04,500 --> 00:01:16,040
But also the prices at cafes coffee shops restaurants stores everything seems to be quite high very similar to the prices where I'm from in florida.
咖啡馆、餐厅、商店的价格似乎也都很高，和我老家佛罗里达的价格非常相似。

10
00:01:16,040 --> 00:01:28,740
Taxis are also quite expensive and I found it funny that strangers on the street offered to split a cab with me at night after leaving a bar because they wanted to reduce the price.
出租车也很贵。酒吧散场后，街上的陌生人为了省钱提出和我拼车，我觉得很有意思。

11
00:01:28,740 --> 00:01:38,479
You could pay around 11 to 20 euro within dublin city center for like a five or ten minute ride.
在都柏林市中心，坐五到十分钟，可能就要十一到二十欧元；这是作者当时的经历。

12
00:01:38,479 --> 00:01:44,700
And I even paid 30 euro one time because there was no availability of taxis.
有一次我甚至付了三十欧元，因为叫不到其他出租车。

13
00:01:44,700 --> 00:01:49,159
And sometimes the buses can be a bit slow so that was pretty shocking.
有时候公交又有点慢，所以这让我相当吃惊。

14
00:01:49,159 --> 00:01:54,299
Something that was a very pleasant surprise was how good the food was.
一个令人惊喜的地方，是食物比我想象的好吃。

15
00:01:54,299 --> 00:01:58,680
I really wasn't expecting that much as far as the foodie scene.
我本来对这里的美食氛围没有太高期待。

16
00:01:58,680 --> 00:02:07,439
I haven't heard that much of about the scene here in dublin or throughout ireland I was kind of just expecting a lot of burgers and pub food.
我没怎么听说都柏林或爱尔兰的美食情况，本来只预期有很多汉堡和酒吧食物。

17
00:02:07,439 --> 00:02:17,150
And while of course there is plenty of that I was surprised by the variety of food and how many healthy options there were as well.
虽然这些当然不少，但食物种类之多，以及有这么多她认为健康的选项，令她意外。

18
00:02:17,160 --> 00:02:32,520
So if you come to ireland definitely enjoy the local food everything at the cafes like soups sandwiches scones everything seems homemade and made within that location.
所以来爱尔兰可以享受当地食物。咖啡馆里的汤、三明治、司康等，感觉都是店里自己做的。

19
00:02:32,520 --> 00:02:36,650
So that's something that shocked me in a good way.
这是一种让我开心的意外。

20
00:02:36,660 --> 00:02:42,599
Another thing that surprised me was the weather it's actually been like this the entire time I've been here.
另一件让我意外的是天气：我在这里期间一直像这样。

21
00:02:42,599 --> 00:02:49,670
Yeah it's been a little bit windy it's been a little cloudy and cold but it hasn't rained yet the whole time I was here.
是有一点风、一些云，也有点冷，但我在这里一直还没遇到下雨。

22
00:02:49,680 --> 00:03:00,009
And I was expecting it to rain pretty much every day so I've been pleasantly surprised at how mild the weather has been although maybe I just got lucky.
我原本以为几乎天天下雨，所以天气这么温和让我很惊喜，也许只是我运气好。

23
00:03:00,019 --> 00:03:06,530
Something that legitimately blew me away is how friendly the people are in dublin.
都柏林人的友好程度，真的让我惊叹。

24
00:03:06,540 --> 00:03:11,700
Now I've always heard that people are friendly in ireland as they are in many countries.
我一直听说爱尔兰人友好，就像很多国家的人一样。

25
00:03:11,700 --> 00:03:17,400
But I definitely noticed that people see more laid back here.
但我确实注意到，这里的人感觉更加放松；see 的字幕用词待复核。

26
00:03:17,400 --> 00:03:24,300
They also seem to know each other like it seems like a very small town like a big city with a small town feel.
他们似乎也相互认识，感觉像小镇，是一座带着小镇氛围的大城市。

27
00:03:24,300 --> 00:03:31,620
And I've noticed a lot of people like running into each other on the sidewalks greeting each other stopping for a chat.
我注意到很多人在路上偶遇、互相打招呼，停下来聊聊天。

28
00:03:31,620 --> 00:03:37,319
And that's not something that you typically see in big cities people are usually in a hurry.
这不是大城市里通常能看到的情景，大家往往行色匆匆。

29
00:03:37,319 --> 00:03:44,270
But I was definitely surprised by how many people seem to know each other and would just bump into each other on the streets.
所以，看到这么多人似乎相互认识，在街上偶然碰见，我确实感到惊讶。

30
00:03:44,280 --> 00:03:50,509
And then how happy and open they were to talking with foreigners and strangers.
他们还很开心、很愿意和外国人及陌生人交谈。

31
00:03:50,519 --> 00:03:52,850
And so that's something that I really enjoyed.
这是我非常喜欢的一点。
